---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const faqs = [["How many DKIM selectors can a domain have?", "There is no limit. Each selector is a separate DNS TXT record. Domains commonly have 2-5 selectors for different email services and key rotation."], ["Should I delete old DKIM selectors?", "Only after confirming no mail is being signed with the old key. During rotation, both keys coexist. After rotation is complete, the old record can be safely deleted."]];

const article = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: "Multiple DKIM Selectors",
  description: "Multiple DKIM selectors: why domains have several DKIM keys (provider + rotation) and how to manage them.",
  inLanguage: 'en',
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PromptDNS', url: 'https://promptdns.com/' },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PromptDNS', url: 'https://promptdns.com/', logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: 'https://promptdns.com/favicon.svg' } },
  datePublished: '2026-10-27',
  dateModified: '2026-10-27',
};

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map(([q, a]) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: a },
  })),
};

const breadcrumbs = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://promptdns.com/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Email Authentication', item: 'https://promptdns.com/email-authentication/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: "Multiple DKIM Selectors" },
  ],
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Multiple DKIM Selectors: Why Domains Have Several DKIM Keys and How to Manage Them"
  description="Multiple DKIM selectors: why domains have several DKIM keys (provider + rotation) and how to manage them."
  schema={[article, faqSchema, breadcrumbs]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/email-authentication/" class="hover:text-accent">Email Authentication</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">Multiple DKIM Selectors</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">Multiple DKIM Selectors</h1>
    <div class="pd-answer" data-vs="answer">
      <p class="text-lg text-ink-dim">Multiple DKIM selectors explained: why domains have several DKIM keys and how to manage key rotation.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="not-prose my-8" aria-label="Reference table">
      <div class="glass rounded-2xl p-5 shadow-lg sm:p-7 overflow-x-auto">
        <table class='pdns-table' style='width:100%'><thead><tr><th class='whitespace-nowrap'>Selector</th><th class='whitespace-nowrap'>Typical use</th><th class='whitespace-nowrap'>Provider</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='pd-mono'>google</td><td>Google Workspace default signing</td><td>Google Workspace</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>selector1, selector2</td><td>Microsoft 365 DKIM rotation pair</td><td>Microsoft 365</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>k1, k2</td><td>Mailchimp and legacy systems</td><td>Various</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>s1, s2</td><td>Zoho Mail signing keys</td><td>Zoho</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>resend</td><td>Resend email API signing</td><td>Resend</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>default</td><td>Generic or self-hosted mail servers</td><td>Self-hosted</td></tr></tbody></table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <article class="rich-text mt-10 max-w-none">
      <h2>Technical details</h2>
      <p class='mt-3'>Multiple DKIM selectors allow a domain to have several active signing keys simultaneously, each published at a unique selector._domainkey.domain.com DNS location.</p><p class='mt-3'>Key rotation uses paired selectors (e.g., selector1 and selector2): the provider alternates signing between them, allowing the old key to be safely replaced without interrupting email flow.</p><p class='mt-3'>Third-party email services each use their own selector, so a domain using Google Workspace plus SendGrid plus Mailchimp will have three separate DKIM DNS records.</p>

      <aside class="mt-8 rounded-xl border-l-3 border-l-violet/50 bg-violet/5 p-5" aria-label="Practitioner field notes">
        <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-violet mb-2">Field notes</p>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim italic">The mistake I see most often: a client rotates to selector2 but forgets to delete the selector1 DNS record after the rotation is complete. This is harmless (the old key just sits unused), but it clutters DNS and can confuse debugging if the old key is expired or weak.</p>
      </aside>

      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3">
        <details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How many DKIM selectors can a domain have?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">There is no limit. Each selector is a separate DNS TXT record. Domains commonly have 2-5 selectors for different email services and key rotation.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Should I delete old DKIM selectors?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Only after confirming no mail is being signed with the old key. During rotation, both keys coexist. After rotation is complete, the old record can be safely deleted.</p></details>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-8 text-xs text-ink-faint">
        Check your domain with our free tools:
        <a href="/spf-record-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">SPF checker</a>,
        <a href="/dmarc-record-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">DMARC checker</a>,
        <a href="/dkim-record-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">DKIM checker</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
